ls for operators\n\n### Deliverables Summary\n\n| Deliverable | Format | Audience |\n|-------------|--------|----------|\n| Threat Model | PDF Report | Security teams, management |\n| Vulnerability Assessment | PDF + Appendix | Technical teams, vendors |\n| Detection Tool | Open-source repository | Operators, analysts |\n| Hardening Guide | PDF + Config files | System administrators |\n| Training Materials | Slides + Exercises | Operations staff |\n| Final Report | PDF with appendices | All stakeholders |\n\n## References\n\n1. IEC 60870-5-104:2006 - Transmission protocols for power system control and supervision\n2. NIST SP 800-82 Rev. 2: Guide to Industrial Control Systems (ICS) Security\n3. ENISA: Threat Landscape for SCADA and ICS Systems (2023)\n4. MITRE ATT&CK for ICS - T1195 Supply Chain Compromise\n5. ENISA: Cryptographic Security in Industrial Control Systems (2022)\n6. ISA/IEC 62443 Series - Security for Industrial Automation and Control Systems\n7. CISA - Joint Guidance on Securing Critical Infrastructure\n8. OWASP SCADA Security Guide\n9. IEEE 1686/IEC 61850 - Communication Networks and Systems for Power Utility Automation\n10. ISO/IEC 27001 - Information Security Management Systems\n\n---\n\n*This research proposal focuses exclusively on defensive security measures to protect CBRN monitoring systems from malicious firmware modifications, supply chain compromises, and protocol-level attacks. All activities are designed to enhance the resilience and reliability of critical safety monitoring infrastructure.*\nEOF\necho \"Report created successfully.\"\nls -la /app/research/report.md"
